  "commander": "Erebos, God of the Dead",
  "description": "Tests Layer 4 type-changing effects from devotion gods (Theros block: Heliod, Erebos, Thassa, Nylea, Purphoros). Erebos's oracle: 'As long as your devotion to black is less than five, Erebos isn't a creature.' This deck floods with double-pip {B}{B} and triple-pip {B}{B}{B} permanents so devotion regularly crosses the 5-symbol threshold, causing Erebos to flip from enchantment-only to enchantment-creature mid-game. The test verifies that get_effective_types() correctly applies Layer 4 changes when the controller's devotion crosses thresholds in either direction (devotion increases when permanents enter; decreases when they leave). Audit trigger: HYPOTHESIS #12 from the May 20 cascade/snow/sagas audit, which noted no log line confirms devotion type-flip works. After this deck runs in autoplay, grep '[LAYERS] Erebos.*type' or similar for evidence the flip is recognized.",
